{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-riemannian-metric","title":"def:pseudo-riemannian-metric","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":2604,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:pseudo-riemannian-metric","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-field-scalar-products]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:pseudo-riemannian-metric","line":4394,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Pseudo-Riemannian Metric]\n\\label{def:pseudo-riemannian-metric}\n\n\\uses{def:smooth-field-scalar-products}\n\n\n\n\\dcref{ch2:2.7}\n\nA \\emph{pseudo-Riemannian metric} on a smooth manifold $M$ is a smooth field of\nscalar products on $TM$, equivalently a smooth symmetric $2$-tensor $g$ whose\nrestriction $g_p$ to every $T_pM$ is nondegenerate. A \\emph{pseudo-Riemannian\nmanifold} is a pair $(M,g)$ with such a metric.\n\\end{definition}\n\nConstant signature is imposed separately in Definition\n\\ref{def:pseudo-metric-has-signature}.","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Pseudo-Riemannian Metric] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a70736575646f2d7269656d616e6e69616e2d6d6574726963\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asmooth-field-scalar-products\">↗ def:smooth-field-scalar-products</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2.7</span></span><p></p>A <em>pseudo-Riemannian metric</em> on a smooth manifold <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is a smooth field of scalar products on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$TM$\">$TM$</span>, equivalently a smooth symmetric <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$2$\">$2$</span>-tensor <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g$\">$g$</span> whose restriction <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g_p$\">$g_p$</span> to every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_pM$\">$T_pM$</span> is nondegenerate. A <em>pseudo-Riemannian manifold</em> is a pair <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> with such a metric.  <p></p>Constant signature is imposed separately in Definition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Apseudo-metric-has-signature\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-metric-has-signature\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6465663a70736575646f2d6d65747269632d6861732d7369676e6174757265\">3</a>.","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-is-pseudo-riemannian","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-field-scalar-products","title":"def:smooth-field-scalar-products","label":"def:smooth-field-scalar-products"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-is-pseudo-riemannian","title":"prop:riemannian-is-pseudo-riemannian","label":"prop:riemannian-is-pseudo-riemannian"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-metric-signature-at","title":"def:pseudo-metric-signature-at","label":"def:pseudo-metric-signature-at"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:orthono